{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"c":0.30000001192092896,"t":"E RRSA·","y":0.020318021296656164,"w":0.11728394826253252,"x":0.74691358132140862,"h":0.010306242638398078},{"w":0.069958845774332645,"h":0.008720930389296444,"t":"1718867188","c":0.5,"x":0.7716049391467531,"y":0.046511627815394085},{"h":0.013961042756888253,"w":0.11355213165283205,"x":0.11501232530889503,"t":"Audioscripts","y":0.053953778805746477,"c":1},{"h":0.015494203960656816,"c":1,"y":0.09690406079319891,"t":"PART 4","w":0.096987635294596336,"x":0.11714404233245737},{"w":0.68106994628906248,"h":0.013084819375836831,"x":0.11728395663583058,"t":"Labyrinths have existed for well over 4,000 years. Labyrinths and labyrinthine symbols have","y":0.12354651149514229,"c":1},{"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"x":0.11728395867861309,"t":"been found in regions as diverse as modern-day Turkey, Ireland, Greece, and India. There","w":0.66872426350911462,"y":0.13808139522901242},{"t":"are various designs of labyrinth but what they all have in common is a winding spiral path","x":0.11728395146299818,"y":0.15253239099380611,"w":0.66049382527669265,"h":0.013250883392226021,"c":1},{"t":"which leads to a central area. There is one starting point at the entrance and the goal is to","y":0.16715116268425456,"w":0.66666666666666663,"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1,"x":0.11728395051095086},{"x":0.11728393952483894,"y":0.181684334495825,"t":"reach the central area. Finding your way through a labyrinth involves many twists and turns,","h":0.013083107479890832,"c":1,"w":0.68312759399414058},{"t":"but it's not possible to get lost as there is only one single path.","c":1,"y":0.19611307394107369,"x":0.11728395616440376,"h":0.011778563015312216,"w":0.46296295166015622},{"c":1,"w":0.66666666666666674,"t":"In modern times, the word labyrinth has taken on a different meaning and is often used as","x":0.11728395051044629,"h":0.011778563015312105,"y":0.2179034156899804},{"t":"a synonym for a maze. A maze is quite different as it is a kind of puzzle with an intricate","x":0.11723952708410632,"y":0.22983912601908696,"c":1,"w":0.64618082682291667,"h":0.014429755149095391},{"t":"network of paths. Mazes became fashionable in the 15th and 16th centuries in Europe,","y":0.24252840298206946,"h":0.017688920837689914,"x":0.11721230684242395,"c":1,"w":0.64628128051757816},{"t":"and can still be found in the gardens of great houses and palaces. The paths are usually","h":0.01308824372937456,"c":1,"x":0.11728396057281486,"w":0.65637858072916666,"y":0.26017441848474465},{"x":0.11728393952793396,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"w":0.68312759399414069,"t":"surrounded by thick, high hedges so that it's not possible to see over them. Entering a maze","y":0.27470930220501355},{"y":0.28916372176253069,"x":0.11728394235701822,"c":1,"h":0.013250883392226243,"w":0.66460906982421875,"t":"usually involves getting lost a few times before using logic to work out the pattern and find"},{"h":0.011627907185728592,"w":0.68518519083658858,"t":"your way to the centre and then out again. There are lots of dead ends and paths which lead","x":0.11728394770047913,"y":0.30377906966099211,"c":1},{"x":0.11728395960801076,"w":0.66255142211914064,"c":1,"t":"you back to where you started. The word 'maze' is believed to come from a Scandinavian","y":0.31831395338165236,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"x":0.11522634056512014,"c":1,"t":"word for a state of confusion. This is where the word 'amazing' comes from.","h":0.01472320376914027,"y":0.33127208471539826,"w":0.56378601074218748},{"t":"Labyrinths, on the other hand, have a very different function. Although people now often refer","w":0.69135803222656245,"h":0.013250883392226132,"x":0.11728394705036246,"c":1,"y":0.35306242665019827},{"t":"to things they find complicated as labyrinths, this is not how they were seen in the past. The","w":0.68106994628906248,"x":0.11522634434254277,"y":0.36773255799028515,"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"t":"winding spiral of the labyrinth has been used for centuries as a metaphor for life's journey. It","w":0.68106994628906248,"x":0.1172839568140904,"c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132,"y":0.38221436959631383},{"t":"served as a spiritual reminder that there is purpose and meaning to our lives and helped to","y":0.39680232546077088,"h":0.01309166752126667,"w":0.67078191121419273,"c":1,"x":0.11728394146008034},{"h":0.011627907185728592,"y":0.411337209195489,"x":0.11728395776799858,"t":"give people a sense of direction. Labyrinths are thought to encourage a feeling of calm and","w":0.6748971048990885,"c":1},{"y":0.42579505310566246,"t":"have been used as a meditation and prayer tool in many cultures over many centuries.","x":0.11728395429957052,"h":0.011778563015311994,"c":1,"w":0.64197530110677081},{"y":0.44758539485367921,"t":"The earliest examples of the labyrinth spiral pattern have been found carved into stone, from","x":0.11934155272624641,"w":0.68312759399414058,"c":1,"h":0.011778563015311994},{"t":"Sardinia to Scandinavia, from Arizona to India to Africa. In Europe, these spiral carvings","y":0.46220930221902745,"w":0.65020573933919268,"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1,"x":0.11728396149156879},{"x":0.11522632630745648,"w":0.68312759399414069,"c":1,"t":"date from the late Bronze Age. The Native American Pima tribe wove baskets with a circular","h":0.014560564106288698,"y":0.47526501741604177},{"t":"labyrinth design that depicted their own cosmology. In Ancient Greece, the labyrinth spiral","w":0.66666666666666674,"y":0.49116607777563059,"h":0.013250883392226243,"c":1,"x":0.11728395051635668},{"t":"was used on coins around four thousand years ago. Labyrinths made of mosaics were","y":0.50436046499522769,"w":0.63991770426432293,"x":0.11728394615737889,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1},{"x":0.11728395272492506,"y":0.5188457009262889,"w":0.59670781453450528,"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1,"t":"commonly found in bathhouses, villas and tombs throughout the Roman Empire."},{"y":0.54063604267490917,"w":0.65637858072916666,"h":0.013250883392226132,"t":"In Northern Europe, there were actual physical labyrinths designed for walking on. These","c":1,"x":0.11934157372832904},{"y":0.55523255801932225,"w":0.63374486287434895,"x":0.11728394707833294,"h":0.013083107479890832,"t":"were cut into the turf or grass, usually in a circular pattern. The origin of these walking","c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.56976744175419491,"t":"labyrinths remains unclear, but they were probably used for fertility rites which may date back","w":0.68930043538411456,"x":0.11934155175427483,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"x":0.117283950524586,"w":0.66666666666666674,"c":1,"h":0.011778563015312105,"y":0.58421672562280513,"t":"thousands of years. Eleven examples of turf labyrinths survive today, including the largest"},{"t":"one at Saffron Walden, England, which used to have a large tree in the middle of it.","x":0.11728394989355195,"c":1,"y":0.59883720919572692,"w":0.61522633870442711,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"w":0.034979422887166378,"x":0.83333333373474316,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"Q31","y":0.23110465100163236,"c":1},{"h":0.011627907185728592,"y":0.28924418590568224,"x":0.83333333393687814,"w":0.037037035624186254,"t":"Q32","c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Q33","y":0.31831395334968016,"x":0.83333333394292997,"w":0.037037035624186143,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"w":0.037037035624186254,"x":0.83333333393687814,"y":0.41133720914389249,"t":"Q34","h":0.013081395583944833,"c":1},{"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1,"x":0.83333333393687814,"y":0.44767441846382172,"t":"Q35","w":0.037037035624186254},{"y":0.48982558120512065,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"Q36","x":0.83333333401689624,"c":1,"w":0.037037035624186254},{"w":0.037037035624186143,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"Q37","x":0.83333333416321564,"c":1,"y":0.58284883696093459},{"c":1,"x":0.11934156117139272,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"More recently labyrinths have experienced something of a revival. Some believe that","w":0.62757202148437496,"y":0.63953488360121791},{"y":0.65254022029608882,"h":0.016488295983088763,"w":0.66475886027018227,"c":1,"x":0.11721738420106666,"t":"walking a labyrinth promotes healing and mindfulness, and there are those who believe in"},{"y":0.66860465102996647,"h":0.014552004064912638,"w":0.67901234944661459,"c":1,"x":0.11522633546219065,"t":"its emotional and physical benefits, which include slower breathing and a restored sense of"},{"y":0.68313953463387989,"c":1,"h":0.011627907185728592,"w":0.69341562906901044,"x":0.11728395118051547,"t":"balance and perspective. This idea has become so popular that labyrinths have been laid into"},{"y":0.69758539484017157,"w":0.51646092732747395,"x":0.11728393951408113,"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1,"t":"the floors of spas, wellness centres and even prisons in recent years."},{"w":0.65432098388671878,"x":0.11728395239271738,"y":0.71937573604069671,"t":"A pamphlet at Colorado Children's Hospital informs patients that 'walking a labyrinth can","h":0.011778563015312216,"c":1},{"t":"often calm people in the midst of a crisis'. And apparently, it's not only patients who benefit.","x":0.11728394957379275,"w":0.67283950805664061,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944611,"y":0.73401162778737261},{"y":0.74852767954274591,"t":"Many visitors find walking a labyrinth less stressful than sitting in a corridor or waiting room.","w":0.67695475260416671,"h":0.011778563015312216,"c":1,"x":0.11728394045630409},{"t":"Some doctors even walk the labyrinth during their breaks. In some hospitals, patients who","x":0.11728395051246206,"y":0.76295641952377091,"w":0.66666666666666663,"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1},{"y":0.77616279057531146,"x":0.11728395963911036,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"can't walk can have a paper 'finger labyrinth' brought to their bed. The science behind the","w":0.66255142211914064},{"t":"theory is a little sketchy, but there are dozens of small-scale studies which support claims","x":0.11728395221076199,"w":0.66049382527669276,"h":0.013250883392226132,"y":0.79063604245909558,"c":1},{"w":0.63580245971679683,"x":0.11728395523876657,"y":0.80523255801471361,"t":"about the benefits of labyrinths. For example, one study found that walking a labyrinth","h":0.013083107479890721,"c":1},{"w":0.65843622843424476,"y":0.81976744172506877,"x":0.11522633018671134,"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"provided 'short-term calming, relaxation, and relief from anxiety' for Alzheimer's patients.","c":1},{"t":"So, what is it about labyrinths that makes their appeal so universal? Well ...","w":0.5596707661946615,"x":0.11728395835961768,"y":0.84156976732179112,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"w":0.03497942288716635,"t":"100","x":0.11728395099854647,"y":0.86773255798110183},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"Q38","w":0.037037035624186143,"y":0.66860465100676225,"c":1,"x":0.83333333394292997},{"h":0.013081395583944611,"x":0.83333333401689624,"t":"Q39","y":0.7761627905074463,"w":0.037037035624186254,"c":1},{"t":"Q40","x":0.83333333393687814,"w":0.037037035624186254,"y":0.81976744171963567,"h":0.011627907185728703,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.66984496081179823,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","w":0.30619837443033859,"y":0.95314993691982619,"h":0.035152653221247165}]}